==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=[[to]] [[hang]] [[out]] [[to]] [[dry]]|hangs out to dry|hanging out to dry|hung out to dry}}

# {{transitive}} To [[attach]] [[washing]] to a [[clothesline]] to dry.
# {{transitive|idiom}} To [[abandon]] someone who is in [[need]] or in [[danger]], especially a colleague or one dependent.
#*'''2008''', Joe Fiorito, "[http://www.thestar.com/printArticle/310368 Our home-care system '''hangs families out to dry''']," ''Toronto Star'', 7 Mar. (retrieved 23 Aug. 2008),
#*: Without supplemental health insurance, we would have been '''hung out to dry'''.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|abandon}} [[leave someone hanging]]

====Usage notes====
* Often carries an element of betrayal of someone who might have expected protection or assistance.

